WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
JAMIE: Or it's a bet they have to make
regardless of the return,

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:06.080
JAMIE: because falling behind on compute
is existential.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:09.470
RUFUS: That's the other reading. And
both can be true simultaneously.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.888
ALEX: Back to the wider story. Jamie,
you were about to say something

00:00:11.888 --> 00:00:14.127
ALEX: about Llama.

00:00:14.237 --> 00:00:17.766
JAMIE: I want to know what happens if
the next Llama model —

00:00:17.766 --> 00:00:21.295
JAMIE: the one this infrastructure is
being built for — doesn't drive
proportional

00:00:21.295 --> 00:00:24.824
JAMIE: revenue. What's the debt service
on twenty-five billion?

00:00:24.909 --> 00:00:28.889
RUFUS: We don't know the specific rate.
Bloomberg notes it's subject to market

00:00:28.889 --> 00:00:32.869
RUFUS: interest rates and bond pricing
conditions. But even at a conservative
estimate,

00:00:32.869 --> 00:00:36.849
RUFUS: you're talking about a
significant annual obligation.
